========================================================================
FKN ROOT PACKET SHELLS AROUND THE TRANSITIVE TILING
========================================================================
Free tiles are the non-simple interval roots of the fixed-path chamber; shell1 gives the dictator atoms, shell2 their first packet interactions.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
n=4  (m=C(n-1,2)=3 free tiles)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
n=4 shell1: m=3 one-flip atoms
  unique iso classes  = 3 (expect m)
  unique score multisets = 3 (expect m)
  height summary (gap g -> count, c3, H):
    g=1: count=2, c3=1, H=3
    g=2: count=1, c3=2, H=5
n=4 shell2: 3 two-flip packets
  c3 packet law exact on all 3 pairs
  same-end : count=  2, q-signs=(neg=2, zero=0, pos=0), q-range=[-2,-2]
  cross-end: count=  0, q-signs=(neg=0, zero=0, pos=0), q-range=[]
  disjoint : count=  1, q-signs=(neg=0, zero=1, pos=0), q-range=[0,0]

